# Context

## Background
T063 added the live probe but no earlier doc caught up with it.
Verification against 0b22357 found: README.md:4 claimed "The
production service is not contacted" unconditionally and never
mentioned the probe command; docs/security.md contained zero
occurrences of "probe"; docs/research-methods.md still described
warn-and-substitute behavior that checkAnalysisSupport had replaced
with rejection in T067.

## Why This Way
Safety claims are now command-specific. The offline default stays
the headline; the probe is documented as the one operator-initiated
exception, with its opt-in flags named where an operator would look
first (README opening, Network policy in security.md).

## Gotchas
The refusal lists in security.md ("prevents these inputs from") were
left untouched on purpose: they scope to untrusted inputs such as
documents, packs, prompts, and agent output. Probe traffic is
operator-initiated, not input-driven, so the lists stay true.
